# Screenshots taken for a design review. They are OUTPUT, not source: every picture in
# this app is drawn by the code that owns it, and a folder of PNGs of the app is the one
# thing here that goes stale the moment a screen changes. Re-take them instead.
#
# ROOTED, or it also hides `tools/shots/` — a pattern with no leading slash matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which quietly left the export harness untracked.
/shots/
*.zip

# Where `npm run shots` writes the screen and asset export. OUTPUT, for the same reason
# the line above is ignored: it is a folder of pictures of the app, and the app is drawn
# by its own code. Re-run the tool rather than committing a copy that goes stale.
export/
